          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %em Boardman-Vogt resolution
            or
            %em W-construction
            is a particular choice of cofibrant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+operads"} topological operads
            (or
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+operads"} simplicial operads
            or similar). It is closely related to the operation of forming the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dendroidal+homotopy+coherent+nerve"} dendroidal homotopy coherent nerve
            = succeed "-" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+categories"} enriched categories
            \/
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+categories"} simplicial categories
            is accordingly closely related to the ordinary
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+coherent+nerve"} homotopy coherent nerve
          %p
            The construction is a variant of the
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+operad"} free operad
            construction, where the free composites of operations are further labeled by “distances” such that for vanishing distance the free composite is replaced with the actual composite.
          %p
            The original Boardman-Vogt resolution over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            generalizes naturally to a cofibrant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operads"} model structure on operads
            for operads enriched over any suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            that is equipped with a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/comonoid"} comonoidal
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the W-construction on topological operads (
                %a{:href => "#BoardmanVogt"}> BoardmanVogt
                );
            %li
              %p
                the cobar-bar resolution of chain complex operads (
                %a{:href => "#GetzlerJones"}> GezlerJones
                ,
                = succeed ");" do
                  %a{:href => "#GinzburgKapranov"} GinzburgKapranov
            %li
              %p
                the Godement simplicial resolution (
                %a{:href => "#Godement"}> Godement
                )
          %h2#Definition Definition
          %h3#over_
            Over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Top
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Top
          %p
            Over
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
            the BV-resolution works as follows:
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+operad"} topological operad
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+operad"} free operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_*(P)
            has as
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trees"} trees
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            inputs, with each vertex of valence
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                  %mo +
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k+1
            labeled by an element in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(k)
          %p
            The operad
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(P)
            is obtained from this by in addition
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                labeling the inner edges of any tree by
                = succeed "s" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+number"} real number
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℓ
                        %mo ∈
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \ell \in [0,1]
            %li
              %p identifying trees one of whose edges has length 0 with the tree with that edge removed and with the correspnding operad-operation labels composed.
            %li
              %p
                equipping the set of labeled trees with the corresponding quotient of the product topology, to make it into a
                = succeed "." do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
          %p
            There is an evident operad morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} F_*(P) \to W(P)
            obtained by regarding each edge of a tree as being of length 1, and there is an evident morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(P) \to P
            obtained by forgetting all trees and sending their operad-operation-labels to their composite.
          %p The composition
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi F
                    %mo *
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  F_*(P) \to W(P) \to P
          %p
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+of+an+adjunction"} counit
            of the
            = succeed "/forgetful" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+functor"} free
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            between operads and their underlying
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/collection"} collection
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            is degreewise sufficiently nice, this factors that counit as a cofibration followed by a weak equivalence and exhibits
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(P)
            as a cofibrant
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/resolution"} resolution
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
          %h3#general General
          %p
            Write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕋
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/groupoid"} groupoid
            of planar
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/trees"} trees
            and non-planar
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            Fix a suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/interval+object"} interval object
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+operads"} model structure on operads
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tree"} tree
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ⨂
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H(T) := \bigotimes_{e \in E(T)}H
                  \\,,
          %p
            where the tensor product runs over all
            %em internal
            edges of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi D
                  %mo ⊂
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D \subset E(T)
            a subset of internal edges, let
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo ⨂
                    %mrow
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ∖
                      %mi D
                  %mi H
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_D(T) = \bigotimes_{ E(T)\setminus D} H
                  \\,.
          %p
            The acyclic cofibration
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \to H
            induces an acyclic cofibration
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H_D(T) \hookrightarrow H(T)
          %p
            and, by the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo :
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo ≠
                      %mi ∅
                  %msub
                    %mi H
                    %mi D
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^-(T) := \coprod_{D \neq \emptyset} H_D(T) \hookrightarrow H(T)
                  \\,.
          %p
            In a similar fashion, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
            an operad, write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P(T)
            for the tensor product of one copy of its objects of
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P^-(T)
            for the coproduct over all such tensor products where at least one, maybe more,
            %em unary
            vertices are omitted. Also the canonical
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi P
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  P^-(T) \hookrightarrow P(T)
          %p
            is a cofibration. Consider for each
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi T
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mo −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                          %msup
                            %mi P
                            %mo −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %msup
                            %mi H
                            %mo −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi P
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mi H
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo ⊗
                          %msup
                            %mi P
                            %mo −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtd
                          %mo →
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi H
                          %mo ⊗
                          %mi P
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo −
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi T
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\array{
                  H^-(T) \otimes P^-(T) &amp;\to&amp; H^-(T) \otimes P(T)
                  \\\
                  \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                  \\\
                  H(T) \otimes P^-(T) &amp;\to&amp;
                  (H \otimes P)^-(T)
                  }
                  \\,.
          %p This induces a univesal morphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi H
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi P
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo →
                  %mi H
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi P
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi T
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (H \otimes P)^-(T) \to H(T) \otimes P(T)
          %p
            and by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout-product+axiom"} pushout-product axiom
            in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+model+category"} monoidal model category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℰ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{E}
            this, too, is a cofibration.
          .un_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              Define
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W(H,P)
              by induction. Start with setting
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %mi P
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W_0(H,P) := P
                    \\,.
            %p Assume that in each induction step we are given morphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %mi Aut
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi S
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (H(S) \otimes P(S)) \otimes_{Aut(S)} I[\Sigma_n] \to W_{k-1}(H,P)(n)
            %p
              for all trees
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
              with less than
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              internal edges. Using the composition operation in the operad
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              to compose two operation when the edge connecting them carries no
              = succeed "-label," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi H
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msubsup
                      %mi α
                      %mi T
                      %mo −
                    %mo :
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi P
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mrow
                        %mi Aut
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi T
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi I
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %msub
                      %mi Σ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo →
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\alpha_T^- : (H \otimes P)^-(T) \otimes_{Aut(T)} I[\Sigma_n] \to W_{k-1}(H,P)(n)
            %p
              Then in the induction step we define for each
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \in \mathbb{N}
              the object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W_n(H,P)
              by the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushout"} pushout
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mo ,
                                %mi T
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi 𝕋
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi n
                                %mo ,
                                %mi k
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi H
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi P
                            %msup
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                              %mo −
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mrow
                                %mi Aut
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi Σ
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi α
                                  %mi T
                                  %mo −
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi W
                              %mrow
                                %mi k
                                %mo −
                                %mn 1
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi H
                            %mo ,
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %munder
                              %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                                %mo ,
                                %mi T
                                %mo ∈
                                %mi 𝕋
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi n
                                %mo ,
                                %mi k
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi H
                            %mo ⊗
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi T
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %msub
                              %mo ⊗
                              %mrow
                                %mi Aut
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                                %mi T
                                %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi I
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                            %msub
                              %mi Σ
                              %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mrow
                                %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∐
                                %msubsup
                                  %mi α
                                  %mi T
                                  %mo −
                          %mtd
                            %msub
                              %mi W
                              %mi k
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi H
                            %mo ,
                            %mi P
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    \\coprod_{[T], T \in \mathbb{T}(n,k)}
                    (H \otimes P)^-(T)
                    \\otimes_{Aut(T)}
                    I[\Sigma_n]
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\coprod \alpha_T^-}{\to}&amp;
                    W_{k-1}(H,P)(n)
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    \\coprod_{[T], T \in \mathbb{T}(n,k)}
                    (H \otimes P)(T)
                    \\otimes_{Aut(T)}
                    I[\Sigma_n]
                    \&amp;\stackrel{\coprod \alpha_T^-}{\to}&amp;
                    W_{k}(H,P)(n)
                    }
                    \\,,
            %p
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi 𝕋
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{T}
              is the subcategory of trees with precisely
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              inputs and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
              internal edges.
            %p The bottom morphism we feed back into the induction procedure.
            %p
              This gives a sequence of collections, and the W-resolution is its
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/colimit"} colimit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo :
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mrow
                        %munder
                          %mi lim
                          %mo →
                      %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mi W
                      %mi k
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ,
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    W(H,P) := {\lim_{\to}}_k W_k(H,P)
                    \\,.
          %p One shows that this collection naturally carries the structure of an operad, etc. pp.
          .un_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi P
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H \otimes P)(T)
              is to be thought of as the space whose points are tuples consisting of one operation in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi P
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} P
              per vertex in
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi H
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} H
              assigned to the inner edges in
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
            %p
              The object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi H
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi P
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (H \otimes P)^-(T)
              is a similar space, but where some of the labels on the inner edges are omitted.
            %p
              The above pushout identifies points that contain lables of inner edges that are 0 with points in one
              = succeed "-stratum" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi W
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
          %h2#examples Examples
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jim+Stasheff"}> Jim Stasheff
              ‘s
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/A-%E2%88%9E+operad"} A-∞ operad
              is the relative Boardman-Vogt resolution
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo *
                    %mo →
                    %mi Assoc
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W([0,1], I_* \to Assoc)
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Assoc"} Assoc
              in
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Top"} Top
              where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi I
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} I_*
              is the operad for
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pointed+object"} pointed object
              = succeed ")." do
                %a{:href => "#BergerMoerdijkAlgebras"} Berger-Moerdijk
          %h2#references References
          %p The W-construction on topological operads is in
          %ul
            %li#BoardmanVogt
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Michael+Boardman"} Michael Boardman
              and
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Rainer+Vogt"} Rainer Vogt
              %em Homotopy invariant algebraic structures on topological spaces
              , Lect. Notes Math. 347 (1973).
          %p The cobar-bar resolution of chain complex operads is in
          %ul
            %li#GetzlerJones
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ezra+Getzler"}> Ezra Getzler
                , J.D.S. Jones,
                %em Operads, homotopy algebra, and iterated integrals for double loop spaces
                , (1995)
            %li#GinzburgKapranov
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Victor+Ginzburg"}> Victor Ginzburg
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Mikhail+Kapranov"} Mikhail Kapranov
                %em Koszul duality for operads
                , Duke Math. J. 76 (1994) 203–272.
          %p The Godement simplicial resolution is in
          %ul
            %li#Godement
              R. Godement,
              %em Topologie algébrique et théorie des faisceaux
              , no. 13, Publ. Math. Univ. Strasbourg, Hermann, Paris, 1958.
          %p
            The generalization to
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/operad"} operad
          %p
            %em#BergerMoerdijkResolution
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em The Boardman-Vogt resolution of operads in monoidal model categories
              , Topology 45 (2006), 807–849. (
              %a{:href => "http://math.unice.fr/~cberger/BV.pdf"}> pdf
              )
          %ul
            %li#BergerMoerdijkAlgebras
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clemens+Berger"}> Clemens Berger
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ieke+Moerdijk"} Ieke Moerdijk
              %em Resolution of coloured operads and rectification of homotopy algebras
              (
              %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/math/0512576"}> arXiv:math/0512576
              )
          %p
            The Boardman-Vogt-resolution for the operad for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/local+nets+of+observables"} local nets of observables
            in
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopical+algebraic+quantum+field+theory"} homotopical algebraic quantum field theory
            (
            %a{:href => "homotopical+algebraic+quantum+field+theory#BeniniSchenkelWoike17"}> Benini-Schenkel-Woike 17
            ) is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#Yau18
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Donald+Yau"}> Donald Yau
              ,
              %em Homotopical Quantum Field Theory
              (
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1802.08101"}> arXiv:1802.08101
